  "description": "COMVAE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H54 Cl4 Dy4 N6 O12,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.487-3.886 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.08-111.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H54Cl4Dy4N6O14. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
